  body: "# Student eligibility and benefit-specific exceptions\n\n## Authored interpretation\n\nThe captured
    student chapter explains the normal JSA and IS restrictions through different underlying conditions
    and then identifies benefit-specific exceptions.\n\n## Scope and exceptions\n\nStudent status alone
    does not settle entitlement. The selected exception passage continues on PDF page 37 and includes
    course, holiday, family and territorial qualifications; IS categories and transitional lone-parent
    provisions differ. No current student entitlement, loan eligibility or course classification is determined.\n\
    \n## Inspected source passages\n\n- [DMG 30012, PDF page 7](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/660bd8e238f66c001184a8db/dmgch30.pdf#page=7)
    — DMG Vol 6 Ch 30: Students, young claimants and their partners.\n- [DMG 30206, PDF page 36](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/660bd8e238f66c001184a8db/dmgch30.pdf#page=36)
    — DMG Vol 6 Ch 30: Students, young claimants and their partners.\n- [DMG 30207, PDF page 36](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/660bd8e238f66c001184a8db/dmgch30.pdf#page=36)
    — DMG Vol 6 Ch 30: Students, young claimants and their partners.\n- [DMG 30208, PDF page 37](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/660bd8e238f66c001184a8db/dmgch30.pdf#page=37)
    — DMG Vol 6 Ch 30: Students, young claimants and their partners.\n- [Inspected continuation, PDF page
    37](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/660bd8e238f66c001184a8db/dmgch30.pdf#page=37) —
    context for the selected paragraph.\n\n## Evidence and review status\n\nModel-assisted interpretation
    of selected passages in the 15 September 2026 frozen source snapshot. Specialist review is required.
    Source acquisition, source revision, legal effective dates and this record’s authoring time are separate.\n\
    \nThis is an independent experimental publication, not an official DWP document, individual advice,
    an entitlement decision or an executable rule. Machine-extracted text may alter reading order, footnotes
    and characters. No PDF visual inspection, whole-chapter coverage or behavioural evaluation pass is
    claimed by this record.\n\n- `dmg-vol6-ch30`: PDF SHA-256 `1540b54680884fdaa8a71e26fdebe12899d876b459d448198a7c941a37960780`;
    extracted pages SHA-256 `768537aba8259637b2425c4f5359b19a59adee89282078ead1e22f6c4f973665`.\n"
  semantic_relations:
  - target: term/legacy-jsais-study-period
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The source gives separate JSA and IS study-period meanings for entitlement purposes,
      so dates must be resolved within the relevant benefit.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol6-ch30/0040
      quote: "30218 For entitlement purposes only, the period of study 1 begins on the date that the student
        starts\nattending or undertaking the course and ends on\n\n\n1. the last day of the course or\n\
        \n\n2. such earlier date as the student\n\n\n      2.1 abandons the course or\n\n\n      2.2 is
        dismissed from the course.\n\n\n                                                             \
        \                      1 IS (Gen) Regs, reg 2(1)\n\n\nJSA"
      locator: DMG 30218
    - page: page/dmg-vol6-ch30/0040
      quote: "30219 For entitlement purposes only, the period of study 1 is\n\n\n1. the period that the
        student is treated as attending or undertaking the course of study and\n\n\n2. any period of attendance
        by the student at their educational establishment or any period of study\nundertaken by a student
        in connection with their course, which is before or after the period of the course.\n\n\n    \
        \                                                                                     1 JSA Regs,
        reg 4\n\n\nNote: The definition at DMG 30218 and DMG 30219 apply to eligibility only. They should
        not be used for\nany other purpose."
      locator: DMG 30219
  - target: term/legacy-jsa-availability
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The normal JSA student restriction is explained through availability for work, while
      IS uses its prescribed-category condition.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol6-ch30/0036
      quote: "30206 Students (F/T students) are not normally eligible for JSA or IS during the period
        of study. This is\nbecause for\n\n\n1. JSA, they are not regarded as available for employment
        1\n\n\n2. IS, they are not a prescribed category of person2.\n\n\n                           \
        \                  1 JSA Regs, reg 15(a); 2 IS (Gen) Regs, reg 4ZA(1), (2) & Sch 1B\n\n\n\nJSA"
      locator: DMG 30206
